<mxCell id="be-packages_20" value="Dependency rule: arrows point inward. domain imports nothing; usecase imports only domain; interface and infra never import each other. main.ts is the only place that knows both sides." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="890" width="560" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="be-packages_21" value="&lt;b&gt;Notation: UML package diagram&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Folder = package (a source directory). Nested folder = sub-package.&lt;br&gt;Dashed arrow with open head = «import» dependency: the tail package imports the head package.&lt;br&gt;Dashed arrow with hollow triangle = realization: infra implements the repository and service ports declared in domain." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="70" width="520" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
